															<h1 class="entry-title fusion-post-title">Video: What is GMEX Fusion and how does it use both centralised and Blockchain Technology?</h1>										<div class="post-content">
				<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The GMEX Fusion platform combines traditional centralised trading systems, which are currently live in multiple exchanges and post-trade venues, with the latest blockchain technology offering the best of both worlds for exchanges, clearing-houses and other institutions. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">GMEX Fusion delivers options for both decentralised and centralised trading solutions, including mobile and web front-ends, CLOB and RFQ matching models, liquidity management, real-time market surveillance, the ability to connect to third party crypto exchanges and a comprehensive set of market data options. The GMEX order execution API is combined with its matching model to offer a sophisticated and agile trading solution representing the best of traditional centralised and blockchain-powered decentralised solutions combined with blockchain based real-time clearing and settlement.</span>    	</p>
							</div>

												<div class="fusion-meta-info"><div class="fusion-meta-info-wrapper"><span class="vcard rich-snippet-hidden"><span class="fn"><a href="https://www.gmex-group.com/author/sysadmin/" rel="author">sysadmin</a></span></span><span class="updated rich-snippet-hidden">2018-06-21T06:29:45+01:00</span><span>21 June 2018</span><span class="fusion-inline-sep">|</span></div></div>													<div class="fusion-sharing-box fusion-theme-sharing-box fusion-single-sharing-box">
